# What gets uploaded to Cloud Build. Without this file gcloud falls back to .gitignore, which is
# written for a different purpose and gets this wrong in both directions:
#
#   * `data/` there is meant to exclude the repo-root data/ dump, but the pattern is unanchored,
#     so it also swallowed src/data/ -- the pydantic models both ETL images import. A directory
#     exclusion cannot be undone by a file-level negation, so no `!src/data/...` line would have
#     rescued it.
#   * `*.txt` there needs a `!services/*/requirements.txt` negation per service, which is easy to
#     forget when adding one (and has already broken a deploy once).
#
# Anchoring with a leading slash is the point of most of these: /data/ is the root dump,
# src/data/ is source.

.git
.github
.gitignore

# Python / tooling noise
.venv
venv
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.vscode
.idea

# Local-only state. /data/ is the root raw-data dump (ThetaData pulls, exports); src/data/ is
# source code and must NOT match -- hence the leading slash.
/data/
logs
runs
notebooks
test
scripts
research
*.log
*.ipynb

# Secrets never belong in a build context; both jobs read theirs from Secret Manager.
.env
.env.*

# Large artefacts
*.pdf
*.png
*.parquet
*.csv
*.sqlite3
